{"at":"2026-10-24T16:36:32.873Z","call":"code-review#1#1","role":"reviewer","step":"code-review","attempt":1,"kind":"text","text":"- **`src/cart.ts`**: `total` sums an array with a `for` loop. The loop condition is `i <= items.length`, so it runs one step past the last valid index.\n","block":"code-review#1#1:m2b1"}
{"at":"2026-10-24T16:36:33.057Z","call":"code-review#1#1","role":"reviewer","step":"code-review","attempt":1,"kind":"text","text":"- **`src/main.ts`**: calls `total([1,2,3])` and prints the result. The call site itself is fine.\n\n","block":"code-review#1#1:m2b1"}
{"at":"2026-10-24T16:36:33.325Z","call":"code-review#1#1","role":"reviewer","step":"code-review","attempt":1,"kind":"text","text":"The bug is in the loop bound. On the final iteration `i` is 3, `items[3]` is `undefined`, and `sum += undefined` makes `sum` `NaN`. So `total([1,2,3])` returns ","block":"code-review#1#1:m2b1"}
{"at":"2026-10-24T16:36:33.567Z","call":"code-review#1#1","role":"reviewer","step":"code-review","attempt":1,"kind":"text","text":"`NaN` and `main.ts` prints `NaN` instead of `6`. Any non-empty array is affected, and an empty array returns `NaN` too, because `items[0]` is `undefined`.\n\n","block":"code-review#1#1:m2b1"}
{"at":"2026-10-24T16:36:33.895Z","call":"code-review#1#1","role":"reviewer","step":"code-review","attempt":1,"kind":"text","text":"The fix is to change `<=` to `<`. Since I can't run the code, this is from reading alone; the factory's test run will confirm it.","block":"code-review#1#1:m2b1"}
